        "knowledge_point": "Differentiating an Inverse Sine Function",
        "problem": "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x) = 5\\arcsin(3x^2).$",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsin x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(3{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3{x}^{2})^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{4}}}\\cdot (6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{30x}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
